  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Science Applications International obligated $2.9B in FY2026 to date across 858 awards, with an average award size of $3.4M. Science Applications International obligations are down 34.9% year over year. Science Applications International received larger totals in prior fiscal years: FY21 was $3.3B, FY22 was $3.9B, FY23 was $4.4B, FY24 was $4.5B, and FY25 was $4.4B. Science Applications International drew the largest FY2026 to date buying share from the Department of Defense, which obligated $1.2B, followed by the General Services Administration at $934M. Science Applications International won the most business in Engineering Services at $1B and in Computer Systems Design Services at $993M. Science Applications International also recorded notable obligations in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences categories, at $225M and $173M respectively, and in several manufacturing and IT services NAICS markets.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Science Applications International's federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Science Applications International obligations fell 34.9% year over year. Science Applications International obligations by fiscal year were $3.3B in FY21, $3.9B in FY22, $4.4B in FY23, $4.5B in FY24, $4.4B in FY25, and $2.9B in FY26 to date. Science Applications International current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date figures."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top customers and markets for Science Applications International?",
        "body": "Department of Defense is the largest buyer of Science Applications International with $1.2B in obligations, followed by General Services Administration at $934M. Engineering Services and Computer Systems Design Services are the top markets for Science Applications International at $1B and $993M respectively, with additional concentrations in R&D, manufacturing of search and navigation systems, and other IT services."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Science Applications International make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Science Applications International made $2.9B from federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Science Applications International has 858 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $3.4M, and obligations are down 34.9% year over year compared with prior years."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Science Applications International?",
      "a": "Department of Defense buys the most from Science Applications International, obligating $1.2B in FY2026 to date. General Services Administration is the next largest buyer at $934M, followed by Department of Homeland Security at $167M, Department of the Treasury at $131M, and Department of State at $123M, with other federal buyers including Department of Transportation, Department of Commerce, Department of Veterans Affairs, Department of Justice, and Department of Health and Human Services."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Science Applications International sell to the government?",
      "a": "Science Applications International sells engineering and IT services and R&D to the government. Science Applications International obligations are concentrated in Engineering Services at $1B and Computer Systems Design Services at $993M, with additional work in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $225M and $173M, plus work in manufacturing and other computer-related services."
    },
